USC: 16-bit selects on vec34

A MOVC testing a 16-bit integer was IMOVC_I16, which only the scalar cores
have: on SGX543 the assembler refused it ("The movc instruction isn't
supported on this core"), e.g. in fma, ldexp and the float4 fmax(x, s).
AppendMovcI16 shifts the test source into the upper half and tests it with
the 32-bit MOVC there, which keeps the sign and zero tests.  It's used for
16-bit min/max, abs and MOVCBIT.

